(5687942, 827653, 64446, '<td valign="top">Nice abstraction and colors...</td>', 'Nice abstraction and colors...', '2009-10-15 00:25:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687947, 827697, 108525, '<td valign="top">Perfect exposure, and I love the colors.<br/>Since you have the upright glass partialy filled, you should adjust your composition a bit.  If you were to pull both glasses toward the camera the blue table would make it look like the upside down glass was filled to the same amount.</td>', 'Perfect exposure, and I love the colors.Since you have the upright glass partialy filled, you should adjust your composition a bit.  If you were to pull both glasses toward the camera the blue table would make it look like the upside down glass was filled to the same amount.', '2009-10-15 00:36:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687949, 827700, 108525, '<td valign="top">This is an awesome shot!  Certainly a different take on the routine "drop of water" shot.  The problem I have is with meeting the challenge criteria.  The light does not seem artificial.  The background looks like a landscape with trees and mountains.  When I look at this photo I see a sunset illuminating it. The challenge description said "to try and make it look artificial".</td>', 'This is an awesome shot!  Certainly a different take on the routine "drop of water" shot.  The problem I have is with meeting the challenge criteria.  The light does not seem artificial.  The background looks like a landscape with trees and mountains.  When I look at this photo I see a sunset illuminating it. The challenge description said "to try and make it look artificial".', '2009-10-15 00:40:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687950, 827520, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great detail and color! I think I would have tried to get the stem pointing directly at the upper right corner.</td>', 'Great detail and color! I think I would have tried to get the stem pointing directly at the upper right corner.', '2009-10-15 00:43:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687951, 827368, 108525, '<td valign="top">I think I would have used a slightly deeper DoF.  You did as normal and focused on the near eye, but that eye is in such a dark shadow it disappears.  I think in this case both eyes and nose should be in proper focus.</td>', 'I think I would have used a slightly deeper DoF.  You did as normal and focused on the near eye, but that eye is in such a dark shadow it disappears.  I think in this case both eyes and nose should be in proper focus.', '2009-10-15 00:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687953, 827239, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great exposure, and DoF.<br/>there are a few parts of the composition I would try and correct in this photo:<br/>I think I would position myself more left.  this would bring the right corner of the "yellow brick road" to the far right lower corner of the photo. This would also bring the left side of the bridge into the frame, and the near lamppost would end up on the left imaginary "thirds" line.<br/>Finally I would cool down the White balance slightly, and rotate the photo counter clockwise a couple degrees to level the bridge out.</td>', 'Great exposure, and DoF.there are a few parts of the composition I would try and correct in this photo:I think I would position myself more left.  this would bring the right corner of the "yellow brick road" to the far right lower corner of the photo. This would also bring the left side of the bridge into the frame, and the near lamppost would end up on the left imaginary "thirds" line.Finally I would cool down the White balance slightly, and rotate the photo counter clockwise a couple degrees to level the bridge out.', '2009-10-15 00:50:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687954, 827661, 108525, '<td valign="top">I would adjust the hue and white balance in this photo. <br/>It seems there is an animal or something causing a distracting motion blur coming off the arm of the couch.<br/>Also, There is now clear subject in this photo. I''m not sure where or what to look at.</td>', 'I would adjust the hue and white balance in this photo. It seems there is an animal or something causing a distracting motion blur coming off the arm of the couch.Also, There is now clear subject in this photo. I''m not sure where or what to look at.', '2009-10-15 00:53:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687959, 827494, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great exposure and comp! I would just crop a bit off the right side of the photo.</td>', 'Great exposure and comp! I would just crop a bit off the right side of the photo.', '2009-10-15 01:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687963, 827451, 108525, '<td valign="top">I think it was smart to use a monochromatic sceme in this photo.</td>', 'I think it was smart to use a monochromatic sceme in this photo.', '2009-10-15 01:18:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687975, 827625, 108525, '<td valign="top">I like this photo a lot! Great exposure.<br/>I do think you need either a little more lamp or little more human.  Right now you are not quite equal, with a bit more lamp offsetting the photo.<br/>I think it would be best to bring the lamp back a few inches, and include just a lil'' more human so that the space between them is in the center of the photo.<br/>I do think it would also work to have unequal amounts of one subject or the other. It would just need to be 2/3 of one and 1/3 of the other.</td>', 'I like this photo a lot! Great exposure.I do think you need either a little more lamp or little more human.  Right now you are not quite equal, with a bit more lamp offsetting the photo.I think it would be best to bring the lamp back a few inches, and include just a lil'' more human so that the space between them is in the center of the photo.I do think it would also work to have unequal amounts of one subject or the other. It would just need to be 2/3 of one and 1/3 of the other.', '2009-10-15 01:36:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687976, 827579, 108525, '<td valign="top">This photo doesn''t really appear to be using artificial light.</td>', 'This photo doesn''t really appear to be using artificial light.', '2009-10-15 01:37:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687977, 827543, 108525, '<td valign="top">The photo is very dark, and it''s hard to make out the subjects when they are so very tiny.</td>', 'The photo is very dark, and it''s hard to make out the subjects when they are so very tiny.', '2009-10-15 01:38:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687978, 827684, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great exposure! I just wish the light didn''t end so abruptly on the stem</td>', 'Great exposure! I just wish the light didn''t end so abruptly on the stem', '2009-10-15 01:39:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687985, 827460, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great composition and exposure!  I would maybe play with the white balance a bit and warm it up a tad.</td>', 'Great composition and exposure!  I would maybe play with the white balance a bit and warm it up a tad.', '2009-10-15 01:56:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687986, 827558, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great twist on the customary "CFL bulb" shot (pun intended)<br/>I think I would try using a deeper DoF to pull the rear twists into focus.</td>', 'Great twist on the customary "CFL bulb" shot (pun intended)I think I would try using a deeper DoF to pull the rear twists into focus.', '2009-10-15 01:58:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687989, 827655, 108525, '<td valign="top">Looks like you chose to shoot at the same locale as another entry.<br/>I think this photo would do better as a 16:10 landscape crop.  I would crop the top down to the far end of the path....leaving out all the "christmas lights".</td>', 'Looks like you chose to shoot at the same locale as another entry.I think this photo would do better as a 16:10 landscape crop.  I would crop the top down to the far end of the path....leaving out all the "christmas lights".', '2009-10-15 02:02:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687991, 827034, 108525, '<td valign="top">this is a cool technique. I just wish your relection stood out a bit more.  It took me awhile to figure out what I was seeing.</td>', 'this is a cool technique. I just wish your relection stood out a bit more.  It took me awhile to figure out what I was seeing.', '2009-10-15 02:05:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687992, 827515, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great composition and exposure.  I wish it were a tad warmer so her face wasn''t quite so blue.</td>', 'Great composition and exposure.  I wish it were a tad warmer so her face wasn''t quite so blue.', '2009-10-15 02:05:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687993, 827518, 108525, '<td valign="top">I think a slight fill light behind the book (if that''s what it is) would help.  Its hard to tell what you are holding.  There is just a hard line across your chest.</td>', 'I think a slight fill light behind the book (if that''s what it is) would help.  Its hard to tell what you are holding.  There is just a hard line across your chest.', '2009-10-15 02:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5687995, 827191, 108525, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors, DoF, and exposure!  <br/>I think I would have panned the frame left just a bit.  This would have caused the right side of the frame to terminate on the tan column of brick, and the left side to include the whole entryway.  Both termination points would give the photo better composition.</td>', 'Beautiful colors, DoF, and exposure!  I think I would have panned the frame left just a bit.  This would have caused the right side of the frame to terminate on the tan column of brick, and the left side to include the whole entryway.  Both termination points would give the photo better composition.', '2009-10-15 02:11:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688001, 827308, 108525, '<td valign="top">Great exposure and color.  the white balance seems spot on!<br/>Whats bothering me is the portrait crop. Everything in the photo (aside from the main bright road) spreads out horizontaly.....the clouds, the mountains, the buildings, etc...<br/> <br/>you could keep the portrait crop if you were to use a tight portrait crop like a 16:10.  If you did that, I would put the near end of the main road in the very lower right corner.</td>', 'Great exposure and color.  the white balance seems spot on!Whats bothering me is the portrait crop. Everything in the photo (aside from the main bright road) spreads out horizontaly.....the clouds, the mountains, the buildings, etc... you could keep the portrait crop if you were to use a tight portrait crop like a 16:10.  If you did that, I would put the near end of the main road in the very lower right corner.', '2009-10-15 02:17:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688002, 827640, 108525, '<td valign="top">Absolutely beautiful!  I just wish I could tell it was artificial light.</td>', 'Absolutely beautiful!  I just wish I could tell it was artificial light.', '2009-10-15 02:17:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688003, 827571, 108525, '<td valign="top">I wish you had a deeper DoF, or didn''t have the distracting blobs in your background.</td>', 'I wish you had a deeper DoF, or didn''t have the distracting blobs in your background.', '2009-10-15 02:18:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688006, 827597, 108525, '<td valign="top">great perspective and composition.</td>', 'great perspective and composition.', '2009-10-15 02:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688007, 827425, 108525, '<td valign="top">A bit too much contrast, and it doesn''t appear to be artificial lighting</td>', 'A bit too much contrast, and it doesn''t appear to be artificial lighting', '2009-10-15 02:36:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688008, 827703, 108525, '<td valign="top">excellent composition, DoF, exposure, white balance ......beautiful!!  One of my favorites in this challenge</td>', 'excellent composition, DoF, exposure, white balance ......beautiful!!  One of my favorites in this challenge', '2009-10-15 02:38:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688010, 827312, 108525, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot, but the flower and bottle seem slightly out of focus</td>', 'I like this a lot, but the flower and bottle seem slightly out of focus', '2009-10-15 02:39:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688011, 827288, 108525, '<td valign="top">I think I would use a portrait crop to get rid of the dead space on the right. Or, a deeper DoF could be used to bring the, I''m assuming, monitor in as a clear part of the composition.  The "monitor" looks like it could be a door, wall, chair, etc.....<br/>I would also incease the color saturation a bit.</td>', 'I think I would use a portrait crop to get rid of the dead space on the right. Or, a deeper DoF could be used to bring the, I''m assuming, monitor in as a clear part of the composition.  The "monitor" looks like it could be a door, wall, chair, etc.....I would also incease the color saturation a bit.', '2009-10-15 02:42:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688013, 827691, 108525, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot.<br/> <br/>I wish the flower on the right was in better focus</td>', 'I like this a lot. I wish the flower on the right was in better focus', '2009-10-15 02:43:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688015, 827631, 108525, '<td valign="top">great lighting.<br/>I think it''s lacking a bit of contrast.</td>', 'great lighting.I think it''s lacking a bit of contrast.', '2009-10-15 02:45:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688017, 827701, 108525, '<td valign="top">this is a cool technique.</td>', 'this is a cool technique.', '2009-10-15 02:45:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688018, 827070, 108525, '<td valign="top">an almost perfect capture. The shutter speed seems tad slow, and the DoF a bit shallow.</td>', 'an almost perfect capture. The shutter speed seems tad slow, and the DoF a bit shallow.', '2009-10-15 02:48:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688019, 827271, 108525, '<td valign="top">this photo could have benefited from a secondary light soucrce to highlight the detail of the subject.</td>', 'this photo could have benefited from a secondary light soucrce to highlight the detail of the subject.', '2009-10-15 02:49:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5688021, 827464, 108525, '<td valign="top">I would like to see how this photo was done in a single exposure and not motion blur.<br/>It''s a great photo with great exposure and perfect composition.</td>', 'I would like to see how this photo was done in a single exposure and not motion blur.It''s a great photo with great exposure and perfect composition.', '2009-10-15 02:50:52.000000', NULL, 1);
