(5692356, 827028, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks like a bit of work went into this one. It paid off.</td>', 'Looks like a bit of work went into this one. It paid off.', '2009-10-19 14:34:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692358, 827425, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like your processing of this, but the composition seems odd. Just too much empty space on the right makes it seem awkward to me. Not sure what you are trying for with the title either, except perhaps being silly. Not that the title really matters for this challenge.</td>', 'I like your processing of this, but the composition seems odd. Just too much empty space on the right makes it seem awkward to me. Not sure what you are trying for with the title either, except perhaps being silly. Not that the title really matters for this challenge.', '2009-10-19 14:39:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692360, 827451, 83313, '<td valign="top">Grthlth!</td>', 'Grthlth!', '2009-10-19 14:42:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692363, 827435, 83313, '<td valign="top">It''s really an alien abduction. They have visited before. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=788671" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">I have proof.</a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=668975" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">More proof.</a></td>', 'It''s really an alien abduction. They have visited before. I have proof. More proof.', '2009-10-19 14:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692366, 827683, 83313, '<td valign="top">In this case the blown highlight work for the image. Not sure all will appreciate how you did it, however.</td>', 'In this case the blown highlight work for the image. Not sure all will appreciate how you did it, however.', '2009-10-19 14:46:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692375, 826528, 83313, '<td valign="top">Just on the off chance that nobody else has left an explanatory comment to accompany their low vote, I will. Hope this helps.<br/> <br/>-The image is pretty soft, could use sharpening.<br/> <br/>-Colors are washed out, some levels and curves adjustments could help that.<br/> <br/>-There is an afterimage that looks like a partial reflection, but it is not obvious enough for me to take it as an intentional part of the composition.<br/> <br/>-You should use the entire 640 pixels available on at least one side. You get  maximum detail into the image that way.<br/> <br/>-Watch the JPEG compression as well, you have up to 150k to use and the less compression you use the clearer your image will be.</td>', 'Just on the off chance that nobody else has left an explanatory comment to accompany their low vote, I will. Hope this helps. -The image is pretty soft, could use sharpening. -Colors are washed out, some levels and curves adjustments could help that. -There is an afterimage that looks like a partial reflection, but it is not obvious enough for me to take it as an intentional part of the composition. -You should use the entire 640 pixels available on at least one side. You get  maximum detail into the image that way. -Watch the JPEG compression as well, you have up to 150k to use and the less compression you use the clearer your image will be.', '2009-10-19 14:54:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692383, 827464, 83313, '<td valign="top">Clearly an intentional effort, but the busy background has nothing to do with the skateboarder and makes it come off like a snapshot. The subject is almost lost in it.  If you could have gotten this same shot from another perspective, it could be very effective.</td>', 'Clearly an intentional effort, but the busy background has nothing to do with the skateboarder and makes it come off like a snapshot. The subject is almost lost in it.  If you could have gotten this same shot from another perspective, it could be very effective.', '2009-10-19 14:57:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692389, 827573, 83313, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of a photographic project from the 80''s, where they took a <a href="//www.amazon.com/Red-Couch-Portrait-America/dp/0912383178/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&amp;s=books&amp;qid=1255975174&amp;sr=1-1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">red couch around the US</a> and photographed it with different places and people.</td>', 'Reminds me of a photographic project from the 80''s, where they took a red couch around the US and photographed it with different places and people.', '2009-10-19 15:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
